# --- Rust ---------------------------------------------------------------
target/
# `rust/Cargo.lock` IS committed. We ship a cdylib, but the wheel we publish is
# a binary artifact: without a lock file, dependency resolution varies by build
# time and platform, which is exactly what the declared MSRV is supposed to
# rule out. `MANIFEST.in` and `rust/Cargo.toml` both already claimed it was
# shipped; now it actually is.
# Rust analyzer / IDE leftovers.
**/*.rs.bk

# --- DuckDB / SQLite (database artifacts) ------------------------------
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.duckdb.tmp
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.db-journal

# --- Raw genomics inputs (large; never commit) -------------------------
# Top-level / bench-level / data-level ignores. Test fixtures under
# tests/data/ are explicitly RE-INCLUDED below so the suite keeps working.
*.fa
*.fasta
*.fai
*.fna
*.bam
*.bai
*.cram
*.crai
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.bcf
*.bed.gz

# Genomics annotations: ignore everywhere except the curated test corpus.
*.gff
*.gff3
*.gtf
*.gff.gz
*.gff3.gz
*.gtf.gz

# Re-include the small curated test fixtures so they stay versioned.
#
# These negations must reach the WHOLE tree, not just its top level. The
# previous form was `!tests/data/*.gff3` + `!tests/data/*.gtf`, and `*` does
# not cross a `/` -- so every fixture under `tests/data/upstream/` and
# `tests/data/v1/` stayed ignored. Twenty-three files the differential suite
# depends on existed only on the machine that created them: a fresh clone or a
# CI runner could not run the parity suite at all, and because
# `differential.fixture()` called `pytest.skip` on a missing file rather than
# failing, the whole compatibility gate reported green while testing almost
# nothing.
#
# The corpus is 716 KB in total, so vendoring all of it costs nothing and
# removes an entire class of "works on my machine".
!tests/
!tests/data/
!tests/data/**

# ...but not the bytecode cache, which the negation above would otherwise
# re-include (later rules win in gitignore).
tests/data/**/__pycache__/

# --- Bench / scratch artifacts -----------------------------------------
bench/data/
bench/out/
benchmarks/data/
benchmarks/out/
*.log

